{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChSvzp2PxeiVYDKmwFGg9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"decision: approved\n\nI found five low-severity follow-ups and no blockers. The two round 4 blockers (N23 and N24) are fixed.\n\n**Checks you asked about**\n- **No read changed its answer:** focused tests and overlay probes show trees, `HEAD^-`, `A..B` and `A...B` still select.\n- **FIFO:** it still cannot block, and removing `O_NONBLOCK` makes the FIFO test hang and fail. I did not test a device file.\n- **Healthy repositories:** `check` reported zero errors on a healthy root and a subdirectory root. It does report errors on a bare repository, which has no work tree.\n- **L1:** confirmed. `git status`, `git ls-files` and the engine read all move the shared index's modification time.\n\n**Test runs**\n- Focused `cli` and `pose` tests pass, including under `-race -count=3`, and `go vet` on those two packages is clean.\n- Both `validate --strict` reruns **failed** in the sandbox, each with 11 failures and 1 timeout. The causes shown are HTTP 403, ownership refusals on `/var/tmp` and `/home`, runtime hosts that could not start, and a file-mode difference.\n- A full run of `internal/cli` and `internal/pose` also failed, with failures of the same kind and none in the subject's tests. The `validate` entries below therefore rest on the sealed evidence.\n- `review-check` and `closeout-check` were run and are deferred until this attestation is recorded.\n- The final cleanup (`go clean -cache` and removal of `go-build*` directories) completed without errors.\n\n**Defects (all low, follow-up)**\n\n| ID | Location | Defect |\n|---|---|---|\n| N1 | `pose-mcp/internal/cli/report.go:326` | Fragments of absolute paths containing spaces or punctuation still reach the versioned report, contrary to D3. |\n| N2 | `pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_reads_index_test.go:272` | Several guards can be removed without any focused test failing. |\n| N3 | `pose-mcp/internal/cli/check.go:1161` | Pre-existing: a POSE root below the repository top misses modified specs. |\n| N4 | `pose-mcp/internal/cli/report.go:319` | Byte-offset truncation can split a UTF-8 character (from reading the code). |\n| N5 | `pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go:121` | Pre-existing: an `ls-files` failure is silently dropped (from reading the code). |\n\nAll required criteria passed; the evidence and rationale for each are in the block below, which `review draft-check` accepts.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n \"decision\": \"approved\",\n \"findings\": [\n  {\"id\":\"N1\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/report.go\",\"line\":326,\"summary\":\"The versioned report still receives parts of absolute paths, although D3 says every absolute path is replaced. The match stops at spaces, quotes, parentheses, colons, semicolons and commas, so '/home/jane doe/my proj/.git/index' becomes '<path> doe/my proj/.git/index', a quoted dubious-ownership path '/srv/John Smith/repo' becomes '<path> Smith/repo', and '/home/a(b)/x:y' keeps '(b)/x:y'. A path preceded by ':', a backtick or '[' is not replaced at all. A real report over a checkout in 'jane doe proj' wrote '<path> doe proj'. Reproduced with an overlay probe. It needs a failed read and such a path.\",\"action\":\"Replace the known root and index paths literally before the pattern, or omit paths from the report note, and test a checkout path containing spaces\",\"owner\":\"pose-maintainers\",\"review_by\":\"2026-12-26\"},\n  {\"id\":\"N2\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_reads_index_test.go\",\"line\":272,\"summary\":\"Guards with no failing test; each mutation leaves the focused cli and pose tests green: restoring --path-format=absolute, dropping the X^- cut in scopeRevisions, dropping the report note bound, dropping the report stderr warning, the ledger calling ReadOnlyIndex without its context, GitEnglish on the check, lookup or hand-over commands, the memfd write fallback, and privateIndexCopy not preserving the index modification time (the racy-clean test reaches only the memory file on Linux).\",\"action\":\"Add a failing test for each listed guard\",\"owner\":\"pose-maintainers\",\"review_by\":\"2026-12-26\"},\n  {\"id\":\"N3\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/check.go\",\"line\":1161,\"summary\":\"Pre-existing, carried from round 1 and listed as a spec follow-up: with the POSE root below the repository top, git diff --name-only returns top-relative names that the .pose/specs/ prefix filter drops, so a modified spec's ready transition goes unchecked without a finding.\",\"action\":\"Run the ready-transition diff with --relative and test a POSE root below the repository top\",\"owner\":\"pose-maintainers\",\"review_by\":\"2026-12-26\"},\n  {\"id\":\"N4\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/report.go\",\"line\":319,\"summary\":\"Both bounds cut at a byte offset (note[:600] here, said[:gitReadSaidLimit] in git_worktree_reads.go:130), so a non-ASCII file or ref name at the cut leaves invalid UTF-8 in the versioned report or the error. Established by reading the code.\",\"action\":\"Cut at a rune boundary in both places\",\"owner\":\"pose-maintainers\",\"review_by\":\"2026-12-26\"},\n  {\"id\":\"N5\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\",\"line\":121,\"summary\":\"Pre-existing: a failing ls-files in worktree scope selection is dropped without a word, so untracked files can silently leave the selection. It reads the real index after the diff read a copy, so an index failure there needs a change between the two reads or another ls-files failure. Established by reading the code, not reproduced.\",\"action\":\"Return the ls-files failure with Git's standard error\",\"owner\":\"pose-maintainers\",\"review_by\":\"2026-12-26\"}\n ],\n \"prior_findings\": [\n  {\"id\":\"R1-N6\",\"status\":\"not-fixed\",\"evidence\":\"Overlay mutation restoring --path-format=absolute in git_worktree_reads.go leaves the focused cli and pose tests green on Git 2.56.0. Carried in N2.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R1-N7\",\"status\":\"partial\",\"evidence\":\"Removing the failOrWarn on a failed git command now fails TestACorruptIndexIsReportedWithItsCause; removing the report stderr warning (report.go:203) still passes. Carried in N2.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R1-N11\",\"status\":\"not-fixed\",\"evidence\":\"check.go:1132 still runs diff --name-only without --relative and check.go:1161 filters on the .pose/specs/ prefix. Carried in N3.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R2-N15\",\"status\":\"partial\",\"evidence\":\"The note is one line (report.go:317) and bounded (report.go:318), GitReadError bounds stderr (git_worktree_reads.go:129); an overlay probe shows path fragments still reach the report. Carried in N1.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R2-N16\",\"status\":\"partial\",\"evidence\":\"Overlay mutations of the hand-over mark, the plain report LC_ALL=C, the non-repository silence and the report marker now fail tests; ReadOnlyIndex in place of ReadOnlyIndexContext in the ledger and an error on a memfd write failure still pass. Carried in N2.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R3-N17\",\"status\":\"fixed\",\"evidence\":\"git_worktree_reads.go:119-135 keeps all stderr with fatal and error lines first; TestScopeSelectionTellsRevisionsFromIndexFailures and TestGitReadErrorsNameTheirCause pass, and the latter fails when the order is mutated.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R3-N20\",\"status\":\"fixed\",\"evidence\":\"validate_scope.go:175-181 labels only an unresolved revision; an overlay probe over a corrupt index gave 'scope selection over HEAD..worktree: git diff failed: ... index file smaller than expected', with no label or repetition, and mutating the exit-code rule fails TestScopeSelectionKeepsWhatTheDiffAccepts.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R3-N21\",\"status\":\"partial\",\"evidence\":\"Removing the plain report GitEnglish now fails TestIndexFailuresAreNamedInAnyLocale (pt_BR translations are installed here); the ledger context, GitEnglish on check, hand-over and lookup, the report warning and the memfd write fallback mutations still pass. Carried in N2.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R3-N22\",\"status\":\"partial\",\"evidence\":\"report.go:317 replaces absolute paths and report.go:318 bounds the note; mutating the replacement fails TestIndexFailuresAreNamedInAnyLocale, but paths with spaces or punctuation leak fragments (overlay probe). Carried in N1.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R4-N23\",\"status\":\"fixed\",\"evidence\":\"validate_scope.go:109-111 runs the diff first; TestScopeSelectionKeepsWhatTheDiffAccepts passes for the empty tree, HEAD^-, A..B and A...B, and an overlay probe selected HEAD^-1.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R4-N24\",\"status\":\"fixed\",\"evidence\":\"validate_scope.go:176-179 reports a rev-parse failure with its stderr; mutating either the exit-code rule or the stderr hand-over fails TestScopeSelectionKeepsWhatTheDiffAccepts.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R4-N25\",\"status\":\"fixed\",\"evidence\":\"git_worktree_reads.go:121-128 orders fatal and error lines first; the reverse order fails TestGitReadErrorsNameTheirCause with the long warning.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R4-N26\",\"status\":\"partial\",\"evidence\":\"The pattern at report.go:326 replaces paths outside the root too, but an overlay probe shows fragments of paths with spaces, parentheses or colons remain. Carried in N1.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R4-N27\",\"status\":\"partial\",\"evidence\":\"Removing the range split now fails TestScopeSelectionTellsRevisionsFromIndexFailures; removing the report note bound still passes. Carried in N2.\"}\n ],\n \"sweep\": \"Implementation diff d998cf07..87261262 and the spec; the increment since round 4 (119d0702). Focused cli and pose tests, go vet, and the focused tests under -race -count=3. Overlay probes for revision forms on healthy and corrupt indexes, report path redaction, check on healthy, subdirectory-root and bare repositories, and an inherited GIT_INDEX_FILE. Overlay mutation run over the guards of the change. L1 measured with core.splitIndex: status, ls-files and the engine read all move the shared index mtime. Callers of ReadOnlyIndex, RawGitDiffReadOnly, reportChangedFiles and the ready-transition read. Planned pose tools, both validate runs, and the full cli and pose test packages, whose failures read as sandbox refusals and include none of the subject tests.\",\n \"criteria\": [\n  {\"id\":\"assumption-integrity\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Verified: L1 (measured here), O_NONBLOCK on a FIFO (mutation blocks the test), relative index path joined to the root, exit 1 with no output for an unknown revision. Unverified: behaviour on a Git older than 2.31 (no stand-in, N2) and non-Linux runtime (only sealed cross builds). Accepted: L1. The 512 MiB index bound is now reported by check instead of dropped, as R2 asks.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"backend-concurrency\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Focused tests including atomic index replacement and concurrent reads pass under -race -count=3; the ledger passes its context (untested, N2).\"},\n  {\"id\":\"backend-contracts\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/machine-channel-integration\",\"rationale\":\"No public contract changes outside failure reporting.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"backend-input-errors\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Unsafe revisions are still refused first; trees, HEAD^- and ranges keep their answer; errors are one line and bounded (N4 on the cut).\"},\n  {\"id\":\"backend-integration-impact\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/git-dispatch-snapshot-integrity-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Callers of the changed reads were traced and remain consistent.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"backend-observability\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Check, scope selection and report name the cause; residual path fragments are N1.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"compatibility\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/machine-channel-integration\",\"rationale\":\"reportChangedFiles is internal; the report gains a warning and a one-line note only on failure; check gains a finding only when a read fails (probe: zero errors on healthy and subdirectory roots, errors on a bare repository, which has no work tree). LC_ALL=C changes message language, not listing output. Dropping --path-format widens Git support.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"correctness\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Focused and negative tests pass; full-package failures in this sandbox are ownership, runtime-start and file-mode failures outside the subject.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"design-causality\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-53d11f68d0751c1b\",\"rationale\":\"D2 removes the stat-then-open race behind R1 by judging the opened descriptor. D3 replaces classification of Git text with diff-first and revision resolution after failure, which addresses R2 and the round 3 and 4 causes. D1 follows from measurement. The design assessment reports no structural deltas.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"documentation\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Spec sections, decisions, trace and follow-ups match the code and tests, and code comments match the fallback behaviour. One overstatement: D3 says every absolute path is replaced (N1). No operational doc or scaffold describes these internals.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"operability\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Failures carry Git's fatal lines first, including broken config causes; check findings are localised.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"requirements\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"R1 to R4 and R6 have tests that pass and kill their main guard mutations; R5 is L1, measured. Remaining gaps are N2.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"scope\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Changed files match the declared artifacts and serve R1 to R6; no non-goal is reopened.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"security\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Revisions stay behind safeGitRevRE, which forbids a leading dash; the index is opened without blocking, must be regular and is bounded; the private copy is mode 0600 in a fresh directory; engine reads keep the sanitised Git environment. Path fragments in a failed-read report note are a low disclosure (N1).\"},\n  {\"id\":\"solution-proportionality\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"The change is local: an open helper, a private copy shared with the non-Linux path, one error formatter and one resolver run only after failure. The two replaceable syscall variables serve tests. The choice would be invalidated if Git began writing an index through the /proc descriptor or rev-parse --verify --quiet changed its exit contract.\"}\n ],\n \"tools\": [\n  {\"id\":\"artifact-check\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-validate-read-only-index-followups --strict\",\"rationale\":\"Exit 0; the findings seen are orphan warnings on repository files.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"assess-design\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-53d11f68d0751c1b\",\"rationale\":\"Observed, no deltas.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"assess-discover\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose assess discover --no-persist --component pose-mcp\",\"rationale\":\"Ran.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"assess-integrate\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/git-dispatch-snapshot-integrity-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Rerun reports three unobserved HTTP consumers, none touched by this change.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"assess-tech-debt\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose assess tech-debt --no-persist\",\"rationale\":\"Ran; the scan declares itself incomplete for two unrelated spec files.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"closeout-check\",\"disposition\":\"deferred\",\"rationale\":\"Run: not terminal, awaiting the review conclusion and lifecycle done.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"review-check\",\"disposition\":\"deferred\",\"rationale\":\"Run: awaits this attestation.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"suggest-review\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\",\"rationale\":\"Ran.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"surface-check\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"reachability:pose-mcp/go/delivery-reachability\",\"rationale\":\"Rerun reported zero findings.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"validate\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Relies on the sealed evidence. The sandbox rerun FAILED (236 steps, 224 pass, 11 fail, 1 timeout): HTTP 403, /var/tmp and /home ownership refusals, runtime hosts unable to start, a file-mode difference. None of the failing tests shown belongs to the subject.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"validate\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Relies on the sealed evidence. The sandbox module rerun FAILED (233 steps, 221 pass, 11 fail, 1 timeout) for the same causes; a separate full run of internal/cli and internal/pose showed failures of the same kind and none in the subject tests.\"}\n ]\n}\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":376,"cache_read_input_tokens":184479,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":376},"output_tokens":3,"service_tie